FILE README.md
# Single-module Compose starter (work in progress)

This starter keeps feature and UI code in the `shared` Kotlin module. `androidApp` is the Android application entry point; `iosApp` hosts the shared Compose view in SwiftUI. It is an incomplete variant under development, not yet a finished template.

For Android, configure the SDK in `local.properties` or `ANDROID_HOME`, then run `./gradlew :androidApp:assembleDebug :shared:testAndroidHostTest` (use `gradlew.bat` on Windows). For iOS, open `iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj` on a Mac with Xcode, select a signing team if needed, and run the app. iOS has not yet been validated.

On a fresh checkout, run `node setup.js` (Node.js 18 or newer) and enter the app name, Android application ID, iOS bundle ID and Kotlin package. The script also accepts `--name`, `--android-id`, `--ios-id` and `--kotlin-package` for non-interactive use. Review its changes before committing. Run `node --test tests/setup.test.js` on an unconfigured template checkout to test setup; these template-only tests skip after configuration.

The counter is in `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/example/starter/counter`; the shared MVI store is in the `mvi` package. The example deliberately uses an in-memory simulated request and has no service dependencies. Other variants are available as branches.

See [FEATURES.md](FEATURES.md) for adding and removing features and [MAINTENANCE.md](MAINTENANCE.md) for maintaining variants.
FILE AGENTS.md
# Agent guide

This is a work-in-progress KMP starter, with Android Compose and iOS using the same Compose UI. The Android application is `androidApp`; shared code and features are in `shared`; `iosApp` hosts the shared framework.

Keep feature presentation state and business logic in common Kotlin. Reducers in `MviStore` are synchronous and serialized; commands run independently and must handle expected failures. State is durable; effects are one-shot. Active-only effects are dropped unless a receiver is ready, including when it is busy; queued effects are retained in memory until one receiver consumes them or the store closes. Do not use effects for durable state.

The counter is a removable example. Keep new service integrations opt-in and do not add secrets or local SDK configuration to version control. Run `./gradlew :androidApp:assembleDebug :shared:testAndroidHostTest` and `node --test tests/setup.test.js` for changes affecting these areas. iOS changes require validation on a Mac with Xcode.

Commands are independent by default. In execute, replaceWork(key) opts into cancelling older dispatched work with the same key; cancelWork(key) cancels it explicitly. Use stable, bounded keys and guard against stale results when cancellation cannot stop an operation.
