# Agent guide

This is a work-in-progress KMP starter, with Android Compose and iOS using the same Compose UI. The Android application is `androidApp`; shared code and features are in `shared`; `iosApp` hosts the shared framework.

Keep feature presentation state and business logic in common Kotlin. Reducers in `MviStore` are synchronous and serialized; commands run independently and must handle expected failures. State is durable; effects are one-shot. Active-only effects are dropped unless a receiver is ready, including when it is busy; queued effects are retained in memory until one receiver consumes them or the store closes. Do not use effects for durable state.

The counter is a removable example. Keep new service integrations opt-in and do not add secrets or local SDK configuration to version control. Run `./gradlew :androidApp:assembleDebug :shared:testAndroidHostTest` and `node --test tests/setup.test.js` for changes affecting these areas. iOS changes require validation on a Mac with Xcode.

Commands are independent by default. In execute, replaceWork(key) opts into cancelling older dispatched work with the same key; cancelWork(key) cancels it explicitly. Use stable, bounded keys and guard against stale results when cancellation cannot stop an operation.
